From 0cf7144481ca1a4a71490140a19970ec045118be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Przemyslaw Czarnota <pczarnota@maxlinear.com>
Date: Wed, 6 Apr 2022 10:42:21 +0200
Subject: bridge: add rtnl_link_bridge_delete()

The new function rtnl_link_bridge_delete(), sends a RTM_DELLINK message
just like rtnl_link_delete(), but it appends additional parameters to
the message, thus not causing the kernel to remove the network device.

Instead, the remove operation is carried out on attributes e. g. we
can remove a VLAN from the bridge port. This will call
ndo_bridge_dellink() in the kernel.
---
